course: dictionary
lesson: 13075
title: Fibber and small fibs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A fibber is a person who tells fibs. A fib is a small lie, one that is not very serious. When someone says «You fibber!», they mean you did not tell the truth, but it is probably not a big problem.
explain: «You fibber! You said you had already tidied your room.» This word is playful and gentle, the sort of thing people say at home or in the playground. It is softer than «liar», which sounds much more serious.
explain: Even small fibs can break trust. People feel less sure of you when they find out you have fibbed, so it is always best to tell the truth.
fact: A fibber is a person who tells fibs.
fact: A fib is a small lie that is not very serious.
fact: «Fibber» is an informal word, so people use it with friends and family rather than in formal writing.
fact: «Fibber» is a gentler word than «liar».
fact: Even small fibs can break trust.
exercise: What is a fibber? | *A person who tells small, not very serious lies | A person who has lost their way home | A person who runs very fast | A person who sings loudly in class
exercise: «You fibber! You said the cake was gone before I got home, but I saw it on the table.» Find and copy the word that names someone who tells small lies. | before | *fibber | table | cake
exercise: A parent says «fibber» instead of «liar» to a child who has told a small lie. Why might they choose the gentler word? | Because fibbers always wear hats | Because fibber is a longer word | Because a fibber is always very rich | *Because a fib is a small, not very serious untruth
test: «Grandma asked, "Did you eat the last biscuit?" Sam said, "No," but there were crumbs on his chin. Grandma smiled and said, "Oh, Sam, you fibber!"» What does fibber mean here? | Someone who has a big, funny hat | Someone who is very hungry | Someone who is very tired | *Someone who tells small lies
test: Which of these is an example of a fibber? | *A girl who says her dog ate her homework when it did not | A girl who reads a book at bedtime | A girl who helps her brother tie his shoes | A girl who draws a picture of her dog
exam: «Ella fibbed about finishing her spelling, but later she told her mum the truth.» What is a fibber? | A person who tells very long stories | *A person who tells small lies that are not very serious | A person who is good at spelling | A person who always writes very neatly
